# The CV PDF has to be committed: GitHub Pages has no build step, so the file
# the site links to must exist in the repo. That makes its diffs unreadable by
# default. This driver lets `git diff` show the text that changed instead.
#
# One-time local setup (the config is not carried in the repo, by design):
#     brew install poppler                                  # provides pdftotext
#     git config diff.pdf.textconv "pdftotext -layout - -"
#
# Without that config git falls back to "binary files differ", so this line is
# harmless if you skip it. It does not affect GitHub's web diff view.
*.pdf diff=pdf

# Keep line endings sane for the hand-written sources.
*.html text
*.css  text
*.md   text
*.py   text
